1.0.1 2026-10-16
  - Text files are now plain git files instead of git-annex pointers: 1982 files
    (.json 1377, .tsv 604, .gitignore 1). Their content is unchanged: each file's SHA-256 equals its
    former annex key. Catalogues such as EEGDash read sidecars from the git tree
    without downloading annexed content, so they could not read sampling rate,
    channel count or duration for this dataset.
  - Added .gitattributes so text files stay in git from now on.
  - The 252 eye-tracking sidecars sub-*/ses-*/beh/*_physio.json stay annexed for now:
    with them readable, BIDS validator 2.4.1 (NEMAR CI) crashes on its
    EyetrackingStimulusPresentation check, because these physio files have no
    events file in beh/.
  - .bidsignore: restored its original content "phenotype/" (the file had been
    committed as a git-annex pointer and ".nemar/" was later appended to the pointer).
  - No data file changed: every annexed recording keeps its annex key.
  - This release also carries the unreleased metadata updates of 2026-10-08/09
    listed below (stimuli table, README).

Metadata update 2026-10-08
  - README: mosquito video link corrected from 9w-5wJYVmcw to e0NT9i4Qnak (Sci Data 2026 Table 2, BBBD website, memory-quiz content); see README.
  - Added stimuli/stimuli.tsv and stimuli.json: one row per stimulus task (YouTube id, presented duration, upload length, verified start offset); no media added.
  - README: section 'Stimuli'.
  - dataset_description.json: GeneratedBy entry for this enrichment.
  - stimuli.tsv/README: stim06 = ~90 s of other material + upload 0-178.6 s (gaze vs picture motion).
  - 2026-10-09 README: provenance check of the mosquito id (the authors' first repository commit names e0NT9i4Qnak) and of the enzyme upload length (already 192 s in a July 2022 Wayback capture).
